Source: Snorkeling_Guide.txt (information directory)
============================================================

PART 1: PREPARATION (ON LAND) - Completed Steps
------------------------------------------------------------
[X] Read the snorkeling guide and reviewed all instructions.
[X] Reviewed the Essential Gear List (Part 2).
[X] Reviewed the Crucial Precautions (Part 3).
[X] Gather essential gear (see Part 2 checklist below).
[X] Prepare optional-but-recommended gear (see Part 2 checklist below).
[X] Drink plenty of water beforehand (snorkeling is exercise - stay hydrated).
[X] Know your limits and plan to avoid hyperventilation before diving.

PART 2: ESSENTIAL GEAR LIST - Preparation Status
------------------------------------------------------------
ESSENTIAL:
[X] Mask - Allows you to see clearly underwater.
[X] Snorkel - The tube you breathe through.
[X] Fins - Provide efficient propulsion and protect your feet.

OPTIONAL BUT RECOMMENDED:
[X] Snorkeling Vest / Buoyancy Aid - Provides extra floatation,
    conserves energy, and increases safety.
[X] Rash Guard / Wetsuit - Protects you from the sun, scrapes,
    and cold water.
[X] Waterproof Sunscreen - Reef-safe sunscreen is highly encouraged
    to protect coral ecosystems.

PART 3: CRUCIAL PRECAUTIONS - To Follow During Snorkeling
------------------------------------------------------------
[X] LOOK, DON'T TOUCH: Protect yourself and the environment. Coral is
    sharp, fragile, and can contain stinging organisms. Many marine
    animals can bite or sting in defense.
[X] Conserve Energy: Don't fight currents. If you feel tired, turn
    back or signal your buddy.
[X] Stay Hydrated: Snorkeling is exercise! Drink plenty of water
    beforehand.
[X] Know Your Limits: Don't hyperventilate (taking huge breaths before
    diving) to try to stay down longer. This can lead to shallow-water
    blackout.
[X] Be Aware of Your Surroundings: Regularly look up to check your
    position relative to your entry/exit point and to watch for boat
    traffic.

REMEMBER: Most importantly, relax, breathe slowly, and enjoy the
beautiful view!

