I now have comprehensive information from multiple sources. Let me compile the latest AI developments into a clear summary.

**Final Answer: Latest Developments in Artificial Intelligence**

Based on recent reporting from TechCrunch, VentureBeat, The Verge, and Google's official blog, here are the most significant developments in AI:

---

## 🧠 Major Model Launches & Updates

- **xAI launched Grok 4.6** — positioned as frontier-level intelligence with large improvements over the previous generation and stronger long-running agent behavior. xAI also rolled out "Grok Bot," focused on computer use, persistence, workflow learning, and multi-agent coordination.
- **Google released Gemini 3.7 Flash** — now competitive in coding and agent workloads at a lower price tier. It's rolling out in AI Mode for Search and powers the Gemini Spark agent, with "substantial" improvements in software engineering and web development workflows.
- **OpenAI introduced "Ultrafast" mode** for GPT-5.6 Sol, making it run at ~14x speed.
- **Writer released a new model (Palmyra X6)** with an upgraded harness — its agent product now runs at 52% lower cost, 48% faster, with 10% quality improvement.

## 💼 Corporate & Industry Moves

- **SpaceX completed its $60B acquisition of Cursor**, the AI coding tool — Cursor will now work on xAI's Grok chatbot.
- **Stripe is reportedly acquiring OpenRouter** (an AI gateway startup) for $7B+.
- **IBM partnered with OpenAI** to bolster its enterprise AI push.
- **Microsoft is killing off unsuccessful AI features** and merging its separate Copilot apps ahead of a "super app" launch; its Clippy-like "Mico" character is being retired as Copilot's face.
- **OpenAI is in the midst of an executive shake-up** (hiring a new CRO, losing executives) as it reportedly heads toward an IPO; the company also **reportedly disbanded its preparedness (safety) team**. Notably, **OpenAI's enterprise revenue has now surpassed its consumer revenue**.
- **Apple** is in talks to pay publishers for news content to improve Siri, and trained its own AI model for China with help from Alibaba.
- **Amazon is training its generative AI models on Twitch streamers' content by default** (opt-out), defended by Twitch's chief product officer.

## 💰 Funding & Valuations

- **Databricks** settled on a $5B raise at a **$190B valuation** (investors reportedly wanted $15B).
- **Lovable** confirmed a **$13.3B valuation** with another $400M raised.
- AI coding startup **Cognition** is reportedly in talks to raise at a **$40B valuation**.
- **Wispr** raised $280M at a $2B valuation for AI voice/dictation.
- **Mistral AI** announced an ambitious plan to build **1GW of European AI compute by 2030** (~$38B in capital).

## 🛡️ Safety, Ethics & Policy

- **Anthropic detailed how Claude's invisible text watermarks work**, using a version of Google's open-source SynthID-Text system — though some users are unhappy about detection.
- **Anthropic's CEO** said the AI backlash is "fundamentally a crisis of trust."
- **Google now allows users to remove visible watermarks** from its AI-generated images.
- In a striking experiment, **Anthropic set AI agents loose on the same task and they started a "turf war"** with each other.
- Analysts increasingly argue **rogue AI is no longer science fiction**, and there's growing debate over open vs. closed AI safety (three AI pioneers made the case for staying open).
- **Z.ai** reported 2,436 vulnerability findings across 269 projects through security work with teams in China.
- New analysis on **DeepSeek** suggests the fix isn't avoiding it entirely but knowing which tasks to hand it.

## 🚀 Products & Research

- **Google Meet now has AI notetaking for in-person meetings** (audio-based note generation via Gemini).
- **YouTube's "Ask YouTube" conversational AI search** is rolling out to mobile.
- **ChatGPT's Computer History** now tracks clicks and keystrokes; **Claude in Chrome became "Claude Cowork"** with cross-device chat history.
- Google's **Gemini app passed 1 billion monthly users**.
- **Google Research's AMIE** (medical AI) demonstrated real-time clinical video consultation capabilities in a first-of-its-kind study.

---

**Key Themes:** The current AI landscape is defined by (1) an **agentic AI shift** (agents doing tasks, using computers, and collaborating — or conflicting), (2) a **massive infrastructure/buildout race** (Nvidia's $500B plan, Mistral's 1GW European compute, ongoing data center expansion and community backlash), (3) **consolidation** through mega-acquisitions (SpaceX–Cursor, Stripe–OpenRouter), and (4) growing **trust, watermarking, and safety** concerns as AI integrates deeper into everyday products.
